---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { repoBlob } from "../../lib/links.mjs";
---

<DocsLayout title="Start — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>Start</h1>
    <p class="lede">Open an existing HC-backed Herdr terminal, enter the instruction checkout, and launch your usual interactive coding agent. Give it the task in that same conversation.</p>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Open and launch</h2>
<p>Start the supported Herdr app independently with its matching core. Clone Sum into a separate path, preserving any serving legacy installation.</p><pre class="codeblock" data-language="sh"><code class="language-sh">{`git clone https://github.com/douglasjarquin/sum.git
cd /path/to/sum
codex --no-daemon`}</code></pre><p>For Codex, <code>--no-daemon</code> keeps command execution inside HC. Keep your usual account, model, and permissions. Sum has no executable, build, setup, initialization, or service.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Before delegation</h2>
<p>Read installed <code>hc --skill</code> and the relevant command help. Confirm a real, nonempty <code>HC_TERMINAL_ID</code> and inspect <code>hc get "$HC_TERMINAL_ID"</code> against the matching core. The current conversation must be the actual native lead with status integration and notifications available.</p><p>Successful connection alone is insufficient. An old TUI pane or foreign terminal cannot become a native lead by inventing environment variables. Follow the supported launch path when identity or status support is missing.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/native-hc.md")}> Native prerequisites and qualification limits ↗</a></p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Give the task</h2>
<blockquote>Fix the failing login test in /absolute/path/to/myapp. Keep scope to the bug, run the required checks, arrange independent review, and bring me a PR. Do not merge it.</blockquote><p>The lead can implement directly or brief a bounded helper. Concurrent writers use separate Git worktrees. A helper stays within its assigned role and reports to its immediate parent.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Qualification remains open</h2>
<p>Authenticated native acceptance remains unrun in this change’s API development conversation. Observed versions and CLI help are evidence about inspected artifacts, not a support guarantee.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/ACCEPTANCE.md")}> Native acceptance matrix ↗</a></p>
</div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
